      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "For centuries, the Skwentna River area has been the traditional territory of the Dena'ina Athabascan people, who used its rivers for fishing and hunting.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/skwentna_alaska",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Skwentna sits along the historic Iditarod Trail, serving as a key checkpoint on this renowned route.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/skwentna_alaska",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Skwentna experiences a dry‑summer subarctic climate, with long, cold, snowy winters and short, warm summers, and August temperatures are cooler than June.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Skwentna%2C_Alaska",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Skwentna’s local economy centers on sport fishing, guiding, hunting, ecotourism, small‑scale mining, and logging, with no formal municipal government.",
